/* =============================================================================
   ONE-OFF CLEANUP — delete legacy "Withdrawn" rows  (RUN MANUALLY, ONCE)
   =============================================================================
   The app no longer produces a Withdrawn state: the admin Delete removes a
   person's records outright, and every collection now ignores Withdrawn rows.
   Any rows still carrying Stage1Status = "Withdrawn" are leftovers from the
   earlier soft-withdraw build, and they are exactly the confusing entries the
   status was creating.

   This is DESTRUCTIVE and is deliberately NOT wired into App.OnStart - a delete
   that runs every time the app starts is not something to leave lying around.
   To run it once:

     1. Drop a temporary button on any screen.
     2. Paste the two lines below into its OnSelect.
     3. Preview the app, press it once, check the tables, then DELETE the button.

   Check what you are about to remove first, e.g. put this in a temporary label:
     CountRows(Filter('RolePreference Preferences', Stage1Status = "Withdrawn"))
   ============================================================================ */

RemoveIf('RolePreference PreferenceResponses', Stage2Status = "Withdrawn");
RemoveIf('RolePreference Preferences', Stage1Status = "Withdrawn")
